{"q":"513","t":"Find Bottom Left Tree Value","d":"Medium","p":false,"c":"<p>Given the <code>root</code> of a binary tree, return the leftmost value in the last row of the tree.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"/assets/img/1e6e08af68ed5e0b.jpg\" style=\"width: 302px; height: 182px;\" />\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> root = [2,1,3]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 1\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"/assets/img/a91217e14c44cf9e.jpg\" style=\"width: 432px; height: 421px;\" />\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> root = [1,2,3,4,null,5,6,null,null,7]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 7\n</pre>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>The number of nodes in the tree is in the range <code>[1, 10<sup>4</sup>]</code>.</li>\n\t<li><code>-2<sup>31</sup> &lt;= Node.val &lt;= 2<sup>31</sup> - 1</code></li>\n</ul>\n","h":[],"m":"{\r\n  \"name\": \"findBottomLeftValue\",\r\n  \"params\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"root\",\r\n      \"type\": \"TreeNode\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"return\": {\r\n    \"type\": \"integer\"\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n","g":[{"name":"Tree","slug":"tree"},{"name":"Depth-First Search","slug":"depth-first-search"},{"name":"Breadth-First Search","slug":"breadth-first-search"},{"name":"Binary Tree","slug":"binary-tree"}],"s":[],"co":[["Amazon","amazon"],["Josh Technology","josh-technology"],["Bloomberg","bloomberg"],["Microsoft","microsoft"]]}